    "axes": "+Y up, metres; 2D (x, y) maps to (x, 0, -y)"
  },
  "limits": "Quadratic insertion: suited to thousands of points, not millions. Exact rational arithmetic is used only when the floating-point predicate is too close to call, which is slow for large degenerate inputs. Exact duplicate points are used once. Collinear input raises an error. No constraint edges; see a constrained triangulation for polygons with holes.",
